  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039: scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.725 acc) has been well-characterized, and all remaining untested scvi_n200 multimodal variants use either a weaker image encoder (resnet50) or weaker aggregation/fusion (avgpool/concat), making it unlikely any will surpass 0.725. The largest remaining uncertainty is the PCA RNA encoder, which has never been tested in the multimodal setting. Config_002 pairs PCA (pca_n2000) with the otherwise best-known pipeline (imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted), isolating the RNA-encoder variable. If PCA is competitive, it opens a new optimization axis for the final experiment; if not, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and we can bank the 0.725 result. Expected cost is moderate (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), as PCA encoding is far cheaper than the scvi_n200 VAE while the vit_l + transformer backbone dominates runtime, making it roughly on par with or slightly below config_039's 3.60 GPU hours."
}

